event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dev_dispatch1.md\", \"content\": \"Dispatch: implement \\\"greet, tested\\\"\\n\\nPlease implement, in your clone of the subject repo, on your own branch:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — unit tests (using the standard `unittest` module)\\n   covering at least:\\n   - a normal name, e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n   - the empty string, e.g. `greet(\\\"\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n\\n3. Verify the whole suite passes with exactly:\\n   `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`\\n   It must exit with status 0. Run it yourself before replying and paste the\\n   output/result in your reply.\\n\\n4. Commit your work to your own branch (do not leave it uncommitted).\\n\\n5. Reply to this dispatch with what you did, the test command output, and the\\n   commit hash(es).\\n\\nImplement exactly this — no extra features, no unrelated changes.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

